opennyai_summary.facts:
The present criminal appeal under Section 14-A(2) of the Scheduled Caste and Scheduled Tribes (Prevention of Atrocities) Act, 1989 has been filed against the order dated 25.05.2022 passed by Special Judge, (S.C./S/.T. Act), Firozabad, whereby the learned Judge has rejected the Bail Application No. 1707 of 2022 (Bhisham Pal Vs. State of U.P.) moved on behalf of the appellant in Case Crime No. 77 of 2022 under Sections 323, 376 I.P.C. and Section 3(2)V of S.C./S.T. (P.A.) Act,
Police Station- Eka, District- Firozabad.
It has been submitted on behalf of the appellant that :-
(i) the appellant has been falsely implicated in the present case due to extraneous consideration;
(ii) there is no eye-witness of the incident;
(iii) most of the witnesses whose statements have been recorded u/s 161 Cr.P.C. are relatives of the informant/victim;
(iv) there is no injury on the person of the victim mentioned in the injury report of the victim;
(v) the appellant is in jail since 24.03.2022 and has no criminal history to his credit.
